From: Uke contributors
Subject: [PATCH] clk: qcom: restore the Cliffs camera configuration gates

The Uke OEM GCC enables camera AHB, HF XO and SF XO before publishing
its clocks. The native GCC retained the video gates but omitted these
three camera gates. A NULL always-on clock slot can still satisfy the
consumer clock API; it does not enable the missing GCC registers.

Restore only the exact Uke camera gates, preserving video, display and
GPU policy. Propagate write errors before publication. CAMCC still
verifies its own transport gates and refuses active CRM. No camera bus,
sensor, EEPROM or capture graph is activated here.

OEM: MiCode 5712080a4b0c0b1a879e6d145c601c649ddaddfd,
drivers/clk/qcom/gcc-cliffs.c (GPL-2.0-only; Linux Foundation/Qualcomm).
Same-SoC OnePlus fc892483f1d61f245924681eb5abd563564d9cba is identical.
Electrical cause/effect requires a separate cumulative Uke boot trial.

--- a/drivers/clk/qcom/gcc-cliffs.c
+++ b/drivers/clk/qcom/gcc-cliffs.c
@@ -3171,6 +3171,17 @@ static int gcc_cliffs_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 	if (IS_ERR(regmap))
 		return PTR_ERR(regmap);
 
+	/* Exact Uke OEM camera AHB, HF XO and SF XO configuration gates. */
+	ret = regmap_update_bits(regmap, 0x26004, BIT(0), BIT(0));
+	if (ret)
+		return ret;
+	ret = regmap_update_bits(regmap, 0x26028, BIT(0), BIT(0));
+	if (ret)
+		return ret;
+	ret = regmap_update_bits(regmap, 0x2602c, BIT(0), BIT(0));
+	if (ret)
+		return ret;
+
 	/* OEM requires both configuration gates before any video GDSC access. */
 	ret = regmap_update_bits(regmap, 0x32004, BIT(0), BIT(0));
 	if (ret)
@@ -3180,7 +3191,7 @@ static int gcc_cliffs_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 	if (ret)
 		return ret;
 
-	/* Video bring-up does not force camera/display/GPU gates. */
+	/* Camera/video configuration does not force display/GPU gates. */
 	ret = clk_vdd_proxy_vote(&pdev->dev, &gcc_cliffs_desc);
 	if (ret)
 		return ret;
